{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '35,65p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md\"","aggregated_output":"Its invertibility invariant is:\n\n    decode-db(encode-db(named-datoms))\n      = named-datoms modulo the declared normalization below\n\nThe encoded artifact is a tree-shaped lossless record set, not the linear\ninstruction image. It preserves every `:yin/*` attribute, including\n`:yin/tail?` on every node, `:yin/macro-name`, exact scalar and name spelling,\none source eid for each occurrence, and all semantic references. Decode\nre-merges occurrences by those source eids. It normalizes only emitter-local\ntempids and `t`/`m`; non-`:yin` attributes are retained in a diagnostic side\narea unless the owner declares them irrelevant. Row order is normalized only\ninside the restricted input domain: one fact per entity and attribute and\nexactly one `:yin/root` marker. A batch accepted by named fallback rules\noutside that domain is a diagnostic for this encoding, not silently reordered.\nThis equality is a B0 acceptance test.\n\nThe executable VM promises equivalence with the named semantic VM only after\nnormalization. Results, effects, streams, cursors, stores, terminal and\nblocked outcomes, and errors must agree. Error comparison uses the message\nand normalized ex-data. Closures compare by arity and normalized captured\nvalues; continuations and parked records compare by type and stable identity,\nnot by register layout; stream and cursor references compare by identity; host\nhandles and telemetry are excluded. This normalizer is defined and tested in\nB0, rather than assumed to be an existing repository utility.\n\nThe free environment is the VM's initial environment value, fixed for one VM\ninstance. It is not the mutable callee `:env` register left by an earlier\nnamed `run`. The named VM's environment leak is a separate defect and is not\nsilently included in this contract. B5 either runs both paths with fresh\ninitial environments or records that named-VM defect as a blocking refusal.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
